Coq-BB5
-------

Source: https://github.com/ccz181078/Coq-BB5 (commit 9142e219229baf2245d3f70851947230ea28a318)
Release: Coq-BB5 release v1.0.0, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17061968
Paper: The bbchallenge Collaboration et al., "Determination of the fifth Busy Beaver value",
arXiv:2509.12337, 2025.

* crates/turing-bb/tests/data/BB2_verified_enumeration.csv,
  crates/turing-bb/tests/data/BB3_verified_enumeration.csv and
  crates/turing-bb/tests/data/BB2x3_verified_enumeration.csv are copied unchanged from
  https://docs.bbchallenge.org/CoqBB5_release_v1.0.0/. Their SHA-256 hashes are listed in
  crates/turing-bb/tests/data/README.md.
* The tree normal form enumeration (crates/turing-bb/src/tnf.rs, crates/turing-bb/src/stats.rs)
  and the deciders Loops, n-gram CPS with its history and LRU augmentations, and repeated word
  lists (crates/turing-bb/src/deciders/) are Rust ports of TNF.v, BB4_TNF_Enumeration.v,
  Decider_Loop.v, Decider_NGramCPS.v, Decider_RepWL.v and TM.v of Coq-BB5, with the parameters
  of BB2_Deciders_Pipeline.v, BB3_Deciders_Pipeline.v, BB4_Deciders_Pipeline.v and
  BB2x3_Deciders_Pipeline.v. The ports are not formally verified; their results are compared
  with the Coq-BB5 enumerations node by node.

